Subject: [PATCH] VideoVlcComponent: honour the video's sample aspect ratio

ES sized the RGBA frames it asks VLC for from the track's coded width and
height and ignored the sample aspect ratio. Scraped MAME previews with
non-square pixels then show distorted: galaxian is coded 224x768 with an
18:7 sample aspect (display 3:4) and appeared as a thin vertical strip;
galaga (224x288, 27:28) was 4 % too narrow.

Apply the sample aspect by shrinking one side, so the requested frame has
the display aspect and never more pixels than the source.
--- a/es-core/src/components/VideoVlcComponent.cpp
+++ b/es-core/src/components/VideoVlcComponent.cpp
@@ -9,6 +9,20 @@
 #include <vlc/libvlc_version.h>
 #include <SDL_mutex.h>
 #include <cmath>
+
+// Apply a video track's sample (pixel) aspect ratio by shrinking one side,
+// so the RGBA frames requested from VLC have the picture's display aspect
+// and never more pixels than the source (scraped MAME previews such as
+// galaxian are stored 224x768 with an 18:7 sample aspect).
+static void applySampleAspect(unsigned& width, unsigned& height, unsigned sarNum, unsigned sarDen)
+{
+	if (sarNum == 0 || sarDen == 0 || sarNum == sarDen || width == 0 || height == 0)
+		return;
+	if (sarNum > sarDen)
+		height = std::max(1u, (unsigned)((unsigned long long)height * sarDen / sarNum));
+	else
+		width = std::max(1u, (unsigned)((unsigned long long)width * sarNum / sarDen));
+}
 #include "SystemConf.h"
 #include "ThemeData.h"
 #include <SDL_timer.h>
@@ -750,6 +764,7 @@
 		{
 			mVideoWidth = tracks[track]->video->i_width;
 			mVideoHeight = tracks[track]->video->i_height;
+			applySampleAspect(mVideoWidth, mVideoHeight, tracks[track]->video->i_sar_num, tracks[track]->video->i_sar_den);
 
 			if (hasAudioTrack)
 				break;
